# CHANGELOG.md is normally only edited when a release is cut - individual changes each add their own file
# under changelog.d/ instead (see changelog.d/README.md), which is what stops concurrent pull requests
# conflicting over release notes.
#
# The union merge driver stays as a safety net for the cases that still touch this file directly: two
# release pull requests overlapping, or a contributor adding a note here out of habit (which the assemble
# script deliberately tolerates and folds into the release rather than dropping). Union keeps BOTH sides
# instead of stopping, so such a rebase resolves itself rather than needing a hand-merge of a bullet list.
#
# Note GitHub does not apply this driver when it computes a pull request's mergeability, so a PR touching
# this file can still be shown as conflicting; rebasing locally is what resolves it.
# See https://github.com/orgs/community/discussions/9288
CHANGELOG.md merge=union
